## Required change
The binding says: run the declared `halve` command as a process with the step's whole number and keep its integer stdout as the result. The capture `number` already carries sign and digits together (`-7`), so it is passed straight through as the command's integer argument — exactly like the existing unsigned `halving` definition in `tests/calc/steps/halving.go`, which this negative-case body mirrors. The command is invoked per the declared CLI document (`docs/architecture/calc-cli.yaml`): `go run ./services/calc halve VALUE` from the host root, hence `cmd.Dir = "../.."` relative to the suite directory. Nothing in the body computes a half.

